---
// SSR required: middleware needs to intercept portal.smd.services requests to this path
// and rewrite them to /portal. The prerendered static file would bypass the Worker entirely.
export const prerender = false

// Operator-forward home. Leads on the spine: work is the people you hire and the
// tools you buy, both off the shelf; it always comes back to people, who leave;
// the Operator is the third option, built for your business. Then the Operator
// made concrete, the leash, a secondary consulting path, the founder, one CTA.
// Scope-based consulting moved to /consulting (a clear secondary door),
// not removed. No proof beat here: a pre-launch firm has no honest external
// proof, so the home converts on argument; proof lives in the live demo and in
// real customer references, never a homepage claim or an audit-ledger display.
//
// DRAFT COPY in the inline sections is directional, for the Captain's voice pass.
// Structure, IA, and CTA wiring are final.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro'
import OperatorHero from '../components/OperatorHero.astro'
import ConsultingPath from '../components/ConsultingPath.astro'
import About from '../components/About.astro'
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro'
import CtaButton from '../components/CtaButton.astro'
import { CATEGORY_NAME, CATEGORY_ARTICLE } from '../lib/category'

const categorySchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Product',
  name: 'Operator',
  category: CATEGORY_NAME,
  description:
    'A dedicated Operator, built for your business and given a real role. It takes on the recurring connective work a business would otherwise hire a person to do, on its own isolated infrastructure, with the operating memory it builds belonging to you. Run for you as a flat monthly service.',
  brand: { '@type': 'Brand', name: 'SMD Services' },
  offers: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock',
    seller: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SMD Services' },
  },
}
---

<Base
  title="SMD Services | The Operator, Built For Your Business"
  description="You hire people and you buy tools. Both come off the shelf. The Operator is a third option: a worker built for how your business runs, and run for you as a flat monthly service."
>
  <Nav />
  <main id="main" role="main">
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(categorySchema)} />

    <OperatorHero />

    <!-- § 02 The problem: people and tools come off the shelf; it always comes back to people -->
    <section id="how" class="bg-white px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 02</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          It Always Comes Back To People.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            Work gets done two ways: the people you hire and the tools you buy. But you built your
            business your way, and both of them come off the shelf. So you spend your time bending
            them to fit.
          </p>
          <p>
            And the best tool is only as good as the hand that wields it, so it always comes back to
            people. A new hire takes months to get up to speed. You pay full salary for partial
            value the whole time. And the day they leave, what they learned leaves with them, and
            you start over.
          </p>
          <p>
            None of this is a failure of effort. It is the cost of running your business on things
            that were never built for it. The salary, the ramp, the turnover, the hours spent
            managing it, fixed and rising whether the work is full or slow.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 03 The third option: a worker built for your business; coin the category -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 03</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          Now There's A Third Option.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            Not a person you hire or a tool you buy. A worker, built for your business the way you
            built your business. It is shaped around how you run, it connects to the tools you
            already use, and it learns only your business, never a model shared with everyone else.
          </p>
          <p>
            It is built to wield those tools and work the way you work. As your business changes, it
            keeps learning. And what it learns does not live in one person's head, so it never walks
            out the door. The understanding it builds of how you run is yours.
          </p>
          <p
            class="font-['Archivo'] text-2xl md:text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.01em] leading-tight text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
          >
            We call it {CATEGORY_ARTICLE}
            {CATEGORY_NAME}.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a
              href="/why"
              data-ev="home-why-link"
              class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-['Archivo_Narrow'] text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-primary)] hover:text-[color:var(--ss-color-primary-hover)]"
            >
              <span>Read the full argument for it</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 04 The Operator (our build of the category, made concrete) -->
    <section class="bg-white px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 04</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          Meet The Operator.
        </h2>
        <div
          class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)] mb-12"
        >
          <p>
            The Operator is ours. Picture a remote worker sitting at a desk in your business, with
            access to the systems and processes you already run. You hand it work the way you hand
            work to anyone on your team, and it comes back with the result.
          </p>
          <p>
            Say you give it intake. It reads a new inquiry, pulls the details that matter, drafts
            the first reply in your voice, books the call, and logs it where your team can see. The
            work moves the way it always did. The person doing it changed.
          </p>
        </div>
        <CtaButton variant="secondary" href="/operator" data-ev="home-operator-learn"
          >See how the Operator works</CtaButton
        >
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- § 05 The leash (control + trust; the team behind the worker is the product) -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-4"
          >§ 05</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-10 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)]"
        >
          You Set The Limits. We Keep It Running.
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-8 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-secondary)]">
          <p>
            You decide what the Operator can do on its own and what waits for a person to approve.
            That decision is in writing, it is part of the service agreement, and you can change it
            whenever you want.
          </p>
          <p>
            It starts by watching. When you sign off on a kind of work, it takes that over. Until
            then, its drafts go to a reviewer on your team, who sends them. The Operator cannot give
            itself more authority. Only you can. Every action it takes is recorded where you can see
            it: what it did, when, and why.
          </p>
          <p>
            And keeping it running is our job, not yours. We are the team behind the worker. We
            build it for your business, we wire it into your tools, and we stay accountable for how
            it runs. This is a service, not a download. You are giving feedback to an Operator, not
            taking on a second job managing one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <ConsultingPath />

    <About />

    <!-- § 06 Start the conversation (single primary CTA) -->
    <section class="bg-[color:var(--ss-color-surface-inverse)] px-6 py-24">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl text-center">
        <span
          class="inline-block bg-[color:var(--ss-color-background)] text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-primary)] font-['JetBrains_Mono'] text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] px-2 py-1 mb-8"
          >§ 06</span
        >
        <h2
          class="mb-6 font-['Archivo'] text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black uppercase tracking-[-0.02em] text-white"
        >
          Start The Conversation.
        </h2>
        <p class="mx-auto mb-6 max-w-2xl text-lg text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-muted)]">
          It starts with a conversation. We learn how your operation runs, find the work that is
          eating your team's time, and figure out where a dedicated Operator fits. If the fit is not
          right, we say so.
        </p>
        <p class="mx-auto mb-10 max-w-2xl text-lg text-[color:var(--ss-color-text-muted)]">
          Pricing is a flat monthly subscription, scoped to the role we build together, and we walk
          through it before any setup begins. No hourly billing, no usage meter, no surprise line
          items.
        </p>
        <CtaButton variant="outline-white" href="/book?interest=operator" data-ev="home-final-cta"
          >Start the conversation</CtaButton
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
